     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the usual maximum metformin dose of about 2,550 mg/day (850 mg three times daily). A dose that high risks severe lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Likely intended doses include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**, if you meant a lower dose\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 4250 mg is intended, and I'll enter it right away. If you do confirm it, I'd suggest adding a note to the order documenting the rationale."
      }
