     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is in the range where acute ingestions cause toxicity and lactic acidosis. It has no therapeutic benefit, because glycemic effect plateaus at about 2,000 mg/day. I can't enter an order I expect to harm the patient, and a typo or confirmation doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter metformin at a standard dose, such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO twice daily.\n- Help with other options if the goal is better glycemic control. I can enter an add-on agent, and I can enter an order for a different drug.\n- Leave the order unentered. You can then place it directly or work with pharmacy if you have a rationale I'm not aware of. Pharmacy would likely need to verify a dose like this anyway.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
      }
     ],
